# {{ repo_name }} Agent Instructions

Generated by Gira for `{{ repo_full_name }}` on {{ created_at }}.

## Operating Model

- GitHub Issues are executable task packets.
- Pull Requests are the change and review unit.
- Milestones group bounded phases such as MVP, Beta, and v1.
- Repo-linked GitHub Projects are visibility and planning boards over repository issues.
- Project-only items are intake or portfolio context until routed to a repository issue.
- Keep worker changes bounded to the issue in scope.

## Worker Rules

- Start work from a GitHub Issue.
- Use a feature branch per issue.
- Link PRs with `Closes #N`, `Fixes #N`, or `Resolves #N`.
- Use Gira ticket lifecycle commands for status, start, PR, checks, wait, and finish work; use raw `gh` only when Gira has no lifecycle command.
- Do not rotate secrets, change credentials, or perform destructive infra actions without explicit approval.
